    """ Given a positive floating point number x and an integer n greater than 0,
    compute the n-th power of the number x. Hint: this is similar to computing
    a square (2nd power) of the number, except the exponent is n.
    >>> to_power(2, 5)
    32
    """
    if n == 0:
        return 1
    else:
        return x * to_power(x, n - 1)

